+## 2. Codebase Findings
+
+### Existing Implementations
+- `src/testproject1/rest_api/models/index.py` - `IndexInfo` (SQLModel table). `stamp_reindex_triggered_at(cls, index_id)` (L1125): raw `sa_update(...).values(last_reindex_triggered_at=datetime.now())`, own Session, does not touch `update_date`. `_build_progress_update_kwargs` (L1165) **always** adds `update_date = datetime.now()` to every `update_progress` call, and writes `last_reindex_triggered_at` only if `ProgressUpdate.last_reindex_triggered_at` is set (field exists, L1190). `complete_progress` (L646) and `set_error` (L671) both go through `update_progress` and pass no `last_reindex_triggered_at`. `update_index` (L887) calls `self.update()` (full save, bumps `update_date`) and snapshots `last_reindex_date`.
+- `src/testproject1/datasource/base_datasource_processor.py` - `BaseDatasourceProcessor`. Public entry points all funnel into `process()` (L143): `oversized()` (L383, `_cleanup_data` then `process`), `resume()` (L403), `incremental_reindex()` (L426), and `schedule(background_tasks, func=None)` (L118, calls `_init_index` if `self.index is None`, then queues `datasource_concurrency_manager.run(target, self.index)`). In-memory-only assignments `self.index.last_reindex_triggered_at = datetime.now()` at L224 (success), L244 (guardrail-blocked), L260 (generic error).
+- `src/testproject1/triggers/actors/datasource.py` - scheduled/webhook actors `reindex_code/svn/jira/confluence/google/git_faq/azure_devops_wiki/azure_devops_work_item/xray/sharepoint/xwiki` (all `@with_datasource_job_lock`) each call `IndexInfo.stamp_reindex_triggered_at(payload.index_info.id)` as first statement, then build processor and call `datasource_concurrency_manager.run(processor.oversized | incremental_reindex, processor.index)`. `resume_stale_datasource` (L1116) stamps at L1129. Actors construct processors directly with `index=`/`index_info=`; they do NOT go through `schedule()`.
+- Manual entry points (all start a processor method in a background task):
+  - Code/git: `routers/index/code_repositories.py::update_index_application` (L313) -> `datasource/code/code_datasource_processor.py::update_code_datasource_in_background` (L206; inner `process()` loads IndexInfo, `create_processor`, then `resume()` or `oversized()`; always `oversized` regardless of `full_reindex` flag) -> `run_in_background` (L163).
+  - SVN: `_repository_support.py::_handle_svn_reindex` (L189) -> `datasource/svn/svn_index_service.py::SVNIndexService.reindex` (L55; same inner-`process()` pattern) -> `run_in_background`.
+  - Confluence/Jira/Xray: `routers/index/kb_atlassian.py` (e.g. `update_knowledge_base_confluence` L199) builds processor with `index=kb_index[0]`, then `datasource_processor.schedule(background_tasks, processor.resume | oversized)`. `schedule()` has 22 callers across `kb_atlassian.py`, `kb_azure_devops.py`, `kb_files.py` and 4 more files (not individually opened: `kb_google/kb_git_faq/kb_xwiki/kb_sharepoint` divergence follow the same pattern; verify).
+  - Provider: `routers/index/providers.py::reindex_provider_datasource_index` (L86) -> `background_tasks.add_task(ProviderDatasourceReindexService.run)` (`service/provider/datasource/provider_datasource_reindex_service.py`). This does NOT use `BaseDatasourceProcessor` at all: it calls `ProviderDatasourceAdapter.reindex` (HTTP tool invocation to external provider), `start_progress` if async; completion arrives via provider callback endpoint (`/v1/finalized/index/{id}`, not inspected). Same service is also invoked from `triggers/bindings/webhook.py::handle_datasource`.
+  - File KB: `datasource/file/file_datasource_update_processor.py` overrides `process()` and never sets `last_reindex_triggered_at` (not in the ticket's type list).
+- `src/testproject1/agents/tools/datasource_health_mixin.py::_classify_health`: order is `error -> FAILED`, `not completed -> UNDERNEATH`, `last_reindex_triggered_at > update_date -> STALE`, else `OK`. Used by `SearchKBTool`, code tools (`code/tools.py`, `read_files_tools.py`, `code_clients.py`).
+
+### Architecture and Layers Affected
+- REST routers (`rest_api/routers/index/*`) -> datasource service helpers (`datasource/code/code_datasource_processor.py`, `datasource/svn/svn_index_service.py`) -> processors (`datasource/base_datasource_processor.py` + per-type subclasses) -> model/persistence (`rest_api/models/index.py::IndexInfo`).
+- Parallel path: trigger layer (`triggers/actors/datasource.py`, `bindings/cron.py`, `bindings/webhook.py`) -> processors.
+- Parallel path: provider service layer (`service/provider/datasource/*`).
+- Consumer: agent tools layer (`agents/tools/datasource_health_mixin.py`).
+
+### Integration Points
+- `datasource_concurrency_manager.run` (`datasource/datasource_concurrency_manager.py`) wraps every reindex in both paths; on queue timeout it calls `index_info.set_error`.
+- `update_progress` bumps `update_date` on every progress write during a run, so during a run `update_date` is always later than a trigger-time stamp (health reads UNDERNEATH while `completed=False`, FAILED on `error`).
+- `IndexInfo.filter_by_project_and_repo` re-reads the row inside the background tasks of code/SVN (fresh object).
+
+### Patterns and Conventions
+- Actor pattern: first line of each actor is `IndexInfo.stamp_reindex_triggered_at(payload.index_info.id)`, before any validation.
+- Targeted SQL updates (`sa_update`) are the project convention for fields that must not enforce user edits or bump `update_date` (`try_claim_for_resume`, `stamp_reindex_triggered_at`, `update_progress`).
